.Dd September 23, 2026
.Dt ICE 4D
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ice
.Nd Intel Ethernet 800 Series Device Driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /dev/net/ice*
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver is a GLDv3, multi-threaded, clonable, loadable device driver that
supports the Data Link Provider Interface,
.Xr dlpi 4P ,
on the Intel Ethernet 800 series controllers.
Each PCI physical function is a separate instance.
The link speed follows the attached media and ranges from 100 Mb/s to
200 Gb/s, depending on the controller family and the transceiver or cable.
.Pp
In addition to basic device initialization and the sending and receiving of
frames, the driver supports the following features:
.Bl -dash -offset indent
.It
Jumbo frames up to 9706 bytes.
.It
Promiscuous access via
.Xr snoop 8
and
.Xr dlpi 4P .
.It
IPv4 header checksum offload.
.It
IPv4 and IPv6 TCP and UDP checksum offload.
.It
IPv4 and IPv6 TCP segmentation offload
.Pq LSO .
.It
Receive side scaling
.Pq RSS
across one receive and transmit queue pair per CPU, up to 16 by default.
.It
Transceiver presence and module data.
.It
A port identification LED.
.It
Internal MAC loopback through the
.Sy LB_SET_MODE
loopback ioctls.
.El
.Pp
The
.Nm
driver does not support hardware VLAN filtering, energy efficient Ethernet
.Pq EEE ,
flow control through pause frames, data center bridging
.Pq DCB ,
the precision time protocol
.Pq PTP ,
or SR-IOV.
.Sh SUPPORTED DEVICES
The driver binds every device ID that the Intel common code maps to a
controller family.
Only the E810-C for QSFP
.Pq Sy pciex8086,1592
has been tested on hardware.
The other families are supported by the same code, but they have not been
validated on hardware.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy E810
E810-C and E810-XXV:
.Sy pciex8086,1591 ,
.Sy 1592 ,
.Sy 1593 ,
.Sy 1599 ,
.Sy 159a ,
.Sy 159b .
.It Sy E822
E822-C and E822-L:
.Sy pciex8086,1890
through
.Sy 1894
and
.Sy 1897
through
.Sy 189a .
Not validated on hardware.
.It Sy E823
E823-C and E823-L:
.Sy pciex8086,124c
through
.Sy 124f ,
.Sy 151d ,
and
.Sy 188a
through
.Sy 188e .
Not validated on hardware.
.It Sy E825-C
.Sy pciex8086,579c
through
.Sy 579f .
Not validated on hardware.
.It Sy E830 No and Sy E835
.Sy pciex8086,12d1 ,
.Sy 12d2 ,
.Sy 12d3 ,
.Sy 12d5 ,
.Sy 12d8 ,
.Sy 12da ,
.Sy 12dc ,
.Sy 12dd ,
.Sy 12de ,
.Sy 1248 ,
.Sy 1249 ,
.Sy 124a ,
.Sy 1261
through
.Sy 1263 ,
and
.Sy 1265
through
.Sy 1267 .
Not validated on hardware.
.El
.Sh APPLICATION PROGRAMMING INTERFACE
For each instance, a character-special file
.Pa /dev/net/ice Ns Ar N
is created, where
.Ar N
is the instance number.
The file supports the Data Link Provider Interface
.Pq DLPI ,
which is documented in
.Xr dlpi 4P .
Most consumers should use
.Xr libdlpi 3LIB .
.Pp
The driver also accepts private firmware diagnostic ioctls on this file:
firmware log configuration and log reading, and firmware debug data.
These are not a stable interface.
Only a process in the global zone with the
.Brq Sy PRIV_SYS_DEVICES
and
.Brq Sy PRIV_SYS_CONFIG
privileges can use them, even when a non-global zone owns the link.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The
.Nm
driver always uses auto-negotiation.
Link properties, such as the MTU, are set with
.Xr dladm 8 .
Driver properties are set in the
.Xr driver.conf 5
file
.Pa /kernel/drv/ice.conf
and apply to every instance when it attaches.
.Pp
The driver loads the Dynamic Device Personalization
.Pq DDP
package
.Pa /kernel/firmware/ice/ice.pkg
at attach.
The package enables the full receive and transmit pipeline.
If the package is missing or the device rejects it, the driver enters
.Em safe mode :
it uses one queue pair and withholds checksum offload, LSO and RSS.
The system log records the package that is active.
.Sh PROPERTIES
The following properties may be set in
.Pa /kernel/drv/ice.conf .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy num_queues
A ceiling on the number of receive and transmit queue pairs, from 1 to 127,
the largest ring count that MAC allows in a group.
The driver uses one queue pair per CPU up to this ceiling, limited also by
the queues and MSI-X vectors that the firmware gives the function and by the
vectors that the system grants.
The count need not be a power of two.
A value outside the range is clamped to it and the driver logs a message.
The default is
.Sy 16 .
Each queue pair has its own receive and transmit buffers, so a large count
uses more memory.
.It Sy tx_lso_enable
Set to
.Sy 0
to withhold TCP segmentation offload.
The default is
.Sy 1 .
LSO is never offered in safe mode.
The driver drops an LSO request whose MSS is below 88 bytes, the hardware
minimum.
.It Sy default_mtu
The initial MTU in bytes.
The MTU can also be changed with
.Xr dladm 8
while the link is not in use.
The default is
.Sy 1500 .
.It Sy rx_limit_per_intr
The largest number of frames that one receive ring processes in a single
interrupt before it schedules a throttled software interrupt for the rest.
The value is clamped to the range 16 to 4096.
The default is
.Sy 256 .
.El
.Sh FIRMWARE
The controller runs firmware from its NVM.
The driver reports the controller family, the firmware version and the
admin queue API version in the system log at attach.
.Pp
If the firmware is in recovery mode, the device cannot be used.
The driver posts an
.Sy ereport.io.device.fw_corrupt
event, marks the service as lost, logs a message, and does not attach.
It does the same when the firmware enters recovery mode after a device
reset, and the instance then stays down until the driver is reloaded.
To repair the device, update the NVM with the Intel NVM update tool and
power cycle the system.
If the firmware admin queue API is newer or older than the driver supports,
the driver logs a message and does not attach.
.Sh LED
The port identification LED can blink to locate a port, or follow the link
state under firmware control
.Pq the default .
The driver does not support holding the LED on or off.
The mode is restored after a device reset, and the LED returns to firmware
control when the driver detaches.
If the device refuses that command at detach, the driver logs a message and
detaches anyway; the LED can then blink until the device is reset.
.Sh STATISTICS
The driver provides the standard MAC and Ethernet statistics, and the
following
.Xr kstat 8
entries in module
.Sy ice .
These names are not a stable interface.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy pfstats
Physical port counters: bytes and packets by type, CRC and length errors,
undersize, oversize and jabber frames, MAC faults, and pause frames.
These count every function on the port.
.It Sy vsistats
Counters for the function's own traffic: bytes and packets by type, receive
discards, descriptor shortages, and receive and transmit errors.
.It Sy rx_ring_ Ns Ar N
Per receive ring: bytes and packets, copied and loaned buffers, descriptor
errors, and the checksum verdicts
.Sy rx_hck_v4hdr_ok ,
.Sy rx_hck_v4hdr_err ,
.Sy rx_hck_outer_err ,
.Sy rx_hck_l4_ok ,
.Sy rx_hck_l4_err ,
.Sy rx_hck_v6exthdr ,
.Sy rx_hck_nol4 ,
.Sy rx_hck_unprocessed ,
and
.Sy rx_hck_unknown .
.It Sy tx_ring_ Ns Ar N
Per transmit ring: bytes and packets, copied and bound buffers, drops,
blocked transmits, LSO packets, and the reasons for refused offload requests
.Sy tx_hck_hdrlen ,
.Sy tx_hck_nol3 ,
.Sy tx_hck_nol4 ,
.Sy tx_hck_badl4 ,
.Sy tx_lso_nohck ,
.Sy tx_lso_badhdr ,
and
.Sy tx_lso_badmss .
.El
.Sh FAULT MANAGEMENT
The driver checks register and DMA access with the fault management
framework and posts PCI ereports.
A fatal hardware error, a malicious driver event on this function, or a
failed queue stop causes a function reset; the link reports down until the
reset completes.
If the reset cannot complete, the service is marked lost and the instance
stays down until the driver is reloaded.
.Sh ARCHITECTURE
The
.Nm
driver is supported on
.Sy x86
systems only.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Pa
.It Pa /dev/net/ice*
Per-instance character-special device.
.It Pa /kernel/drv/amd64/ice
Device driver
.Pq 64-bit .
.It Pa /kernel/drv/ice.conf
Driver configuration file.
.It Pa /kernel/firmware/ice/ice.pkg
Dynamic Device Personalization package.
.It Pa /usr/lib/mdb/kvm/amd64/ice.so
.Xr mdb 1
module.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mdb 1 ,
.Xr libdlpi 3LIB ,
.Xr dlpi 4P ,
.Xr driver.conf 5 ,
.Xr dladm 8 ,
.Xr fmadm 8 ,
.Xr kstat 8 ,
.Xr snoop 8
